{"Error handling is too broad - catches errors for both SendGrid API call and database deletion, making it difficult to distinguish which operation failed. If SendGrid cancellation succeeds but database deletion fails, the reminder could remain in database leading to retry attempts": 0.5928832292556763, "Sequential loop for cancelling reminders could become a performance bottleneck with many reminders - each SendGrid API call blocks the next iteration. Should use Promise.all() or p-limit for controlled concurrency": 0.2744745910167694, "Default path marks reminder as cancelled without tracking when this occurred or how many times cancellation has been attempted. Missing metadata fields like cancelledAt, cancelAttempts, and lastCancelError for retry logic and operational visibility": 0.03972151502966881, "SMS reminders are immediately deleted from database while email reminders use deferred cancellation (marking as cancelled for CRON processing) - architectural inconsistency means different failure modes and race conditions between channels": 0.2613156735897064, "Making cancelled field nullable (Boolean?) creates tri-state logic (null/false/true) which complicates queries - WHERE cancelled = true won't match null values, potentially causing bugs. Should migrate to Boolean @default(false)": 0.5153517127037048, "Using immediateDelete: true for emails during reschedule is inconsistent with cancellation flow used elsewhere (handleCancelBooking.ts uses deferred cancellation) - could hit SendGrid's 100 pending cancellation limit during reschedule operations": 0.1530900001525879, "15-minute eventual consistency window creates race condition where reminders scheduled within 15 minutes of cancellation may still be sent before CRON job processes them": 0.46029767394065857, "Missing send-time verification - actual reminder send path should check reminder.cancelled status immediately before sending as defense-in-depth measure": 0.19264864921569824, "No retry mechanisms or observability for failed cancellations - missing error tracking, retry metadata, and backlog monitoring": 0.23783740401268005}